            "review_title": "Review at La Garden Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Karno N\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam385 contributions\n1\nCozy and Charming\nJan 2020\nLạ means different, and it just opened recently. \n\nThe location is off of a busy Nguyen Dinh Chieu street in District 3. Sometime you just have to get away from all the noises which I did.\n\nThe location is very easy to find and accessible by car. On the onset it has this charming looks on the outside with colorful and cozy decor. 1st floor is where the business part of the restaurant is ( seating can be on the outdoor in the evening), and seating start on the 3nd, and 4th. On the way up the narrow staircase you will pass by the kitchen on the 2nd floor. \n\nSeating is spacious with good windows view to the street below and an elementary school across the street.\n\nServices; \nStaffs are well trained and can definitely be recommending you the readily available dishes in the kitchen, or mostly ordered. \n\nFoods;\nLạ serves 2 kind of foods; The local Vietnamese foods such as Spring rolls (which I tried), Hot pots, sticky rice, and steam chicken dishes. And the other is the Western foods such as Hamburger (which I tried), Spaghetti, Fish, and Steak.\n\nFor this visit have ordered, Spring Rolls for appetizer and a Cheese Burger for lunch. The Spring rolls are huge and filling, and the Burger was juicy and dripping with melted cheese and Sauce.. These were delicious and filling. There are other dishes that I would want to come back and try in the near future. \n\nDrinks; there are Wines and Beers available.\n\nBills; the above cost me about 200,000 vnd which is less than $10 usd.\n\nWell, this a cozy little place that has a lot to offer.. good taste and easy on the wallet.\n\nBTW; they are also available on Foody for deliveries.\n\nUntil then, enjoy and safe travels.\n\nK :)\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 12, 2020",
